WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.459 --> 00:00:05.060
Is this the latest pawn in a global power
game?

00:00:05.060 --> 00:00:11.100
Spy novelist and blogger Yang Hengjun was
a Chinese diplomat before he became an Australian

00:00:11.100 --> 00:00:12.100
citizen.

00:00:12.100 --> 00:00:16.100
He flew from the New York to Guangzhou last
week, where he mysteriously dropped off the

00:00:16.100 --> 00:00:17.100
grid.

00:00:17.100 --> 00:00:19.519
Friends raised the alarm when he couldn't
be contacted.

00:00:19.519 --> 00:00:23.919
Beijing at first denied all knowledge of his
whereabouts.

00:00:23.919 --> 00:00:29.069
But now officials have confirmed Yang is in
residential detention in Beijing and has been

00:00:29.069 --> 00:00:33.680
charged with espionage.

00:00:33.680 --> 00:00:36.050
Australia is demanding consular access at
the earliest opportunity.

00:00:36.050 --> 00:00:41.780
It's also seeking urgent clarification as
to whether Yang's detention, is linked to

00:00:41.780 --> 00:00:47.370
Canada's arrest of top Huawei executive Meng
Wanzhou in December.

00:00:47.370 --> 00:00:56.090
China has detained several foreigners since
then, widely seen as retaliation.

00:00:56.090 --> 00:01:00.199
Australian Foreign Minister Marise Payne sees
no evidence of a connection, for the moment.

00:01:00.199 --> 00:01:04.659
I would be concerned if there was an indication
of that.

00:01:04.659 --> 00:01:10.210
So we are calling on the Chinese authorities
to ensure that this matter is dealt with transparently

00:01:10.210 --> 00:01:11.310
and fairly.

00:01:11.310 --> 00:01:15.320
Feng Chongyi, a friend and colleague of Yang's,
says the arrest is clearly linked to what

00:01:15.320 --> 00:01:19.170
he calls, Beijing's "hostage diplomacy".

00:01:19.170 --> 00:01:29.290
Because of the Huawei case, I believe they
are using these people as hostages to exercise

00:01:29.290 --> 00:01:36.390
pressure on Canadian government, on the government
of the United States and the government of

00:01:36.390 --> 00:01:43.710
Australia as well to release Meng Wanzhou
back to China.

00:01:43.710 --> 00:01:47.960
China's recent detention of foreign nationals
is straining its international relations.

00:01:47.960 --> 00:01:53.159
But Beijing appears determined to play hard
ball, in a high-stakes dispute with the West.

